comment.narrative:
Output 1: Strengthened inclusion and transparency of the electoral process.
Target for indicator 1.1: 10% increase in voter registration especially women, youth and PWD.
Target for indicator 1.2: 7.5% increase in female candidates in all direct elective positions.

Output 2: Enhanced institutional capacity for EC and other electoral stakeholders.
Target for Indicator 2.1: 10% Increase in public trust in the EC (i.e. to 52%)
Target for indicator 2.2: Three (3) institutions (EC, judiciary, human rights commission, police & media) with capacity to effectively support electoral processes;
Target for indicator 2.3: A) One (1) ToT (national); B) Five ( 5) operational ToT at (subnational); B) Eleven (11) ToT (Subregional); C) One BRIDGE TtF modular trainings; C) Trainings of Police,Judic.& Media.

Output 3: Strengthened dialogue capacities and electoral violence early warning and rapid response system (EWER)
Target for indicator 3.1: EWER systems at national and district levels in place
Target for indicator 3.2: Two (2 EWER systems partially include gender-data;
Target for Indicator 3.3: Three (3) dialogues held for mediation and consensus building.

Output 4: Effective and efficient management, partnership formation and monitoring and evaluation of the project 
Target for indicator 4.1: Eight (8) Project staff recruited on schedule;
Target for Indicator 4.2: Four (4) Partnerships in place to support the electoral process;
Target for Indicator 4.3: One (1) Project Mid-term Evaluation undertaken;
Target for Indicator 4.4: 75% Annual Resource Delivery.

description.narrative:
This indicator measures the number of training programmes that are to be undertaken to strengthen capacity of the electoral commission and other stakeholders on electoral processes. These trainings include, 
 1)Operational  training  for  EC; a)One ToT (national) and b) 11 ToT    (Sub-regional);   c)    One BRIDGE   TtF&d)   10   BRIDGE modular trainings; 

2) Training of Ministry of Justice and Constitutional Affairs in electoral law/regulation drafting; 3) Operational trainings for the Police, Judiciary and Media.
